### Paired samples 
We have treated the samples as independent however we know this is false as every group submitted a guess for both lecturers ages and so there is dependence between the same groups guesses e.g. one group may be very flattering and more likely for all their guesses to be lower. So naturally the data pairs between the groups guesses, e.g. group 1's guess for Kirsty is 37 and Theo is 35 and that would be a pair


c) We now want to perform a paired test to compare the guesses between Kirsty and Theo, our hypotheses are $H_0:\mu_d=0$ and $H_1:\mu_d\neq 0$, where $\mu_d$ is the population mean difference between paired guesses for Kirsty and Theo. 
      
